system "Retried job"

# A job is retried until it succeeds or runs out of attempts. The attempt
# count belongs to the running state and the reason to the failed one, so
# neither exists when it means nothing.

types
  attempt is an integer from 1 to 3

state
  job is one of queued, running with (attempt is attempt), succeeded, failed with (reason is one of crashed, timed_out)
  tries is an integer from 0 to 3

initially
  job is queued
  tries is 0

always
  job is running implies attempt of job is tries
  job is failed implies tries is 3
never
  job is failed with {reason: timed_out} and tries < 3

sometimes
  job is succeeded
  job is failed with {reason: crashed}
  job is failed with {reason: timed_out}
  job is running with {attempt: 3}

eventually
  job is succeeded or job is failed

fair action start
  requires job is queued
  job becomes running with {attempt: tries + 1}
  tries becomes tries + 1

action succeed
  requires job is running
  job becomes succeeded

action crash
  requires job is running
  job becomes if attempt of job is 3 then failed with {reason: crashed} else queued

action time_out
  requires job is running and attempt of job is 3
  job becomes failed with {reason: timed_out}

scenario "Third time lucky"
  reject succeed
  start
  crash
  start
  expect job is running with {attempt: 2}
  crash
  start
  succeed
  expect job is succeeded and tries is 3
  reject start
